  bootwright / apply
      Realize the complete selected Environment, or continue the exact operation an
      interruption left behind. The plan is always complete; --stage only gates which blocks
      this invocation starts, and the operation pauses at that boundary. --until
      <cluster>.<package> starts only that add-on instance and the blocks it requires, then
      pauses; a later apply continues the rest. Review the plan before confirming; --yes skips
      ordinary confirmation.

  Usage
    bootwright apply [flags]

  Command flags
      --authorize  Acknowledge a planned risk (data-loss, or data-loss=<digest> of the steps
                   the plan shows, required with --yes or without a terminal), or present a
                   rotated access credential at its current version (rebind=<secret>) (values:
                   data-loss)
      --stage      Select comma-separated stages to start (default: all) (values: controller,
                   infrastructure-services, substrates, machines, clusters, add-ons)
      --until      Stop after one add-on instance, named <cluster>.<package>, and the blocks it
                   requires
      --yes        Confirm the command's ordinary confirmation

  Common flags
      --ascii       Use ASCII status markers
      --color       Select terminal colors (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --context     Select a context (default: current context)
      --detail      Select human detail (values: compact, full) · default compact
      -h, --help    Show help for this command
      -o, --output  Select output mode (values: text, json, yaml) · default text
      --progress    Select progress animation (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --width       Set presentation width (0: automatic) · default 0

  More detail
    Use --help --detail full to include SSH overrides.

  Examples
    bootwright apply --context lab --stage machines
